=== Mortality [reciprocal full-data source contrast]
Selected MIMIC-IV full-data runs (44,454 observations): 9d208f03e24644fd84cd6b5f54631ea6, 5a7e9905ab1d4daeb6ebd67210d17e83, 3c68739ace1841578ccab944bd287a4b
Selected EUH full-data runs (16,379 observations): 1b36fb5e05d54ea1ac1827ca8397b1cd, 960fcc8032bc407a9d168e9bd7b620e4, 6b7887e217a6491b98a33ee454d1b2de
Pairing validation:
  Models: the same 10 configured and successfully evaluated instances occur in every selected logical repeat from both sources, including complementary model runs; no exclusions or missing models.
  MIMIC-IV: one cohort fingerprint across every reciprocal run (41df522b11394fa479fe124e4f3e056de18f2b31be3ada3c8d9bd303c217b1af); exact ordered IDs/labels for 11,114 held-out observations; target=mortality, dataset.random_state=1337, dataset.train_size=0.8, evaluation_bootstrap_seed=1337; prediction schema 1/2 order=('mimic', 'tudd'); exact bootstrap IDs 0..9999 (10,000 draws) across both sources and metrics.
  EUH: one cohort fingerprint across every reciprocal run (50e24d458a0d42d786534f80da26b596a391cccdcece0f1a8df3f38890d3f5f1); exact ordered IDs/labels for 4,095 held-out observations; target=mortality, dataset.random_state=1337, dataset.train_size=0.8, evaluation_bootstrap_seed=1337; prediction schema 1/2 order=('mimic', 'tudd'); exact bootstrap IDs 0..9999 (10,000 draws) across both sources and metrics.
LaTeX caption:
\caption{\textbf{Local rather than external full-data training has model-specific effects for Mortality.} Columns fix the held-out MIMIC-IV and EUH evaluation populations; rows show AUROC. Each point is score(the same model trained on the evaluation center's complete pool) minus score(the same model trained on the other center's complete pool), in percentage points, so positive values favor local training and negative values favor external training. The complete pools contain 44,454 MIMIC-IV observations (3 repeated pipeline runs) and 16,379 EUH observations (3 repeated pipeline runs), selected only from runs explicitly configured with training fraction 1.0; this is an all-available-data comparison, not an equal-budget source-effect estimate. Whiskers are 95\% percentile intervals from 10,000 paired test-cohort bootstrap score differences after averaging repeated full-data runs within each training source by draw. They quantify resampling of each fixed held-out cohort, not training-repeat variation; cohort fingerprints, ordered cohort IDs and labels, split settings, bootstrap seed/count/IDs, and prediction-dataset order were required to match before pairing. Circles denote classical baselines and triangles tabular foundation models.}
figure: plots/baseline/mortality/mimic_tudd_source_contrast.pdf

