Cross-cohort caption (roc_auc):
\caption{\textbf{11 of 45 comparisons change hands between the in-domain and the external cohort.} Each cell holds two AUROC win shares for one model pair: the share of 10,000 paired cohort-bootstrap draws in which the row model beat the column model, above the diagonal on the held-out MIMIC-IV cohort and below it on the held-out EUH cohort. Rows and columns follow the shared model order used by the other figures, and the white diagonal separates the two halves. Both triangles read row over column, so a pair whose winner does not change has one warm cell and one cool cell, while a pair that changes hands is warm in both. Cells near 50 are undecided, and a share counts resamples of these cohorts rather than the chance that a model generalizes better.}

Paired difference forest caption:
\caption{\textbf{Effect sizes against one reference model anchor the win shares.} Points are paired AUROC differences against XGBoost, so a positive value means the model beat XGBoost on the held-out MIMIC-IV cohort and a negative value means it lost to it, and the same reading holds on EUH. Whiskers are 95\% percentile intervals from 10,000 aligned cohort-bootstrap draws. The number at the right of each row is the share of those draws in which the model outperformed XGBoost. Circles denote classical baselines and triangles tabular foundation models.}

Rank figure caption (roc_auc):
\caption{\textbf{Average AUROC rank over 60 evaluation blocks: TabPFNv3.5 leads, and 5 of 10 models move at least a rank position between the lowest and the highest setting.} Top panel: Nemenyi critical difference diagram of the average rank over 60 evaluation blocks, one per configuration and held-out cohort, from 30 pipeline runs. Models joined by a bar cannot be separated at $\alpha$ = 0.05 (Friedman p < 0.001), and two average ranks have to differ by 1.75 rank positions to count as separated. Middle panel: average rank per setting, with the model name at the right end. Bottom panel: average rank in the smallest and the largest setting, with the net movement annotated. }
Per-setting rank figure caption (roc_auc):
\caption{\textbf{Per-setting critical difference diagrams show where the overall ranking comes from.} One diagram per configuration level, each with its own Nemenyi critical difference and block count. A setting that contributes only a few blocks cannot separate any pair, which the scale bar makes explicit.}

