\caption{\textbf{Adding local MIMIC-IV observations to the complete EUH training pool changes Mortality performance on the target center.} AUROC on the held-out MIMIC-IV cohort for 10 models, each in its own panel. Measured local counts are 100, 200, 400, 800, 1,600, 3,200, 6,400, 12,800, 25,600, 44,454; the fixed external contribution is the complete EUH pool of 16,379 observations. The solid curve trains on local data only, and the dashed curve trains on the complete external pool plus the same local count. Combined training deliberately has a larger total training count than local-only training. Runs of one cell share their training_sample_seed, so the local-only and combined conditions use the same local observations; points summarize one pipeline run per setting. The grey dashed line repeats that model's externally trained score as the level its local data has to beat; it is a measured reference, not a fitted threshold, and it can be switched off with show_external_baseline in VisualSettings. The local-only curve comes from that center's own single-source sweep (sample_size_mimic_mortality), matched cell by cell on training_sample_seed and realized local count; 22 reference run(s) repeated a size with seeds the augmentation sweep does not share and were left out rather than averaged in. Whiskers are 95\% percentile intervals from 10,000 aligned test-cohort bootstrap draws after averaging repeats within each setting; they quantify held-out cohort resampling uncertainty, not training-repeat variation. Only measured settings are drawn and connected.}
